{"1-6":{"people":[{"id":"joshua-h3091g","name":"Joshua","kind":"person","brief":"A judge","count":1,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":2},{"id":"moses-h4872","name":"Moses","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Amram","count":1,"firstVerse":2}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H5892","lemma":"עִיר","tr":"ir","gloss":"excitement","lang":"h","inPassage":8,"uses":1090},{"base":"H7523","lemma":"רָצַח","tr":"ra·tsach","gloss":"to murder","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":47},{"base":"H5127","lemma":"נוּס","tr":"nus","gloss":"to flee","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":159},{"base":"H4733","lemma":"מִקְלָט","tr":"miq·lat","gloss":"refuge","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":20},{"base":"H1696","lemma":"דָבַר","tr":"da·var","gloss":"to speak: speak","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":1142},{"base":"H1097","lemma":"בְּלִי","tr":"be·li","gloss":"without","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":58},{"base":"H1847","lemma":"דַּ֫עַת","tr":"da·at","gloss":"knowledge","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":92},{"base":"H1350","lemma":"גָּאַל","tr":"ga·al","gloss":"to redeem: redeem","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":104},{"base":"H1818","lemma":"דָּם","tr":"dam","gloss":"blood","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":360},{"base":"H5221","lemma":"נָכָה","tr":"na·khah","gloss":"to smite","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":500}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"NUM","chapter":35,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"You are to have these cities as a refuge from the avenger, so that the manslayer will not die until he stands trial before the assembly.","from":6},{"book":"DEU","chapter":19,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"then you are to set apart for yourselves three cities within the land that the LORD your God is giving you to possess.","from":2},{"book":"DEU","chapter":19,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"You must show him no pity. You are to purge from Israel the guilt of shedding innocent blood, that it may go well with you.","from":2},{"book":"NUM","chapter":35,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Six of the cities you give the Levites are to be appointed as cities of refuge, to which a manslayer may flee. In addition to these, give the Levites forty-two other cities.","from":2},{"book":"NUM","chapter":35,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"designate cities to serve as your cities of refuge, so that a person who kills someone unintentionally may flee there.","from":2},{"book":"NUM","chapter":35,"verse":24,"verseEnd":24,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"then the congregation must judge between the slayer and the avenger of blood according to these ordinances.","from":2},{"book":"DEU","chapter":4,"verse":41,"verseEnd":41,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"Then Moses set aside three cities across the Jordan to the east","from":2},{"book":"DEU","chapter":4,"verse":43,"verseEnd":43,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"Bezer in the wilderness on the plateau belonging to the Reubenites, Ramoth in Gilead belonging to the Gadites, or Golan in Bashan belonging to the Manassites.","from":2}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"exodus-family","title":"Moses and his circle","people":2}]},"7-9":{"people":[{"id":"ephraim-h0669g","name":"Ephraim","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Joseph","count":1,"firstVerse":7},{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":7},{"id":"naphtali-h5321g","name":"Naphtali","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":7},{"id":"gad-h1410g","name":"Gad","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"manasseh-h4519g","name":"Manasseh","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Joseph","count":1,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"reuben-h7205","name":"Reuben","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":9}],"places":[{"id":"galilee-h1551","name":"Galilee","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":7},{"id":"hebron-h2275a","name":"Hebron","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":7},{"id":"kedesh-h6943g","name":"Kedesh","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":7},{"id":"shechem-h7927g","name":"Shechem","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":7},{"id":"bashan-h1316","name":"Bashan","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"bezer-h1221g","name":"Bezer","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"gilead-h1568g","name":"Gilead","kind":"place","brief":"In Manasseh","count":1,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"golan-h1474","name":"Golan","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"jericho-h3405g","name":"Jericho","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"jordan-h3383","name":"Jordan","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"ramoth-h7216h","name":"Ramoth","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":8}],"words":[{"base":"H4294","lemma":"מַטֶּה","tr":"mat·teh","gloss":"tribe: rod","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":252},{"base":"H7153","lemma":"קִרְיַת אַרְבַּע","tr":"qir·yat ar·ba","gloss":"Kiriath-arba","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":18},{"base":"H2022","lemma":"הַר","tr":"har","gloss":"mountain: mount","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":546},{"base":"H1474","lemma":"גּוֹלָן","tr":"go·lan","gloss":"Golan","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"H7216","lemma":"רָאמוֹת","tr":"ra·mot","gloss":"Ramoth","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"H1221","lemma":"בֶּ֫צֶר","tr":"be·tser","gloss":"Bezer","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":5},{"base":"H1551","lemma":"גָּלִיל","tr":"ga·lil","gloss":"Galilee","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":6},{"base":"H6943","lemma":"קֶ֫דֶשׁ","tr":"qe·desh","gloss":"Kedesh","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":12},{"base":"H7684","lemma":"שְׁגָגָה","tr":"she·ga·gah","gloss":"unintentionally","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":19},{"base":"H4334","lemma":"מִישׁוֹר","tr":"mi·shor","gloss":"plain","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":23}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"NUM","chapter":35,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"These six cities will serve as a refuge for the Israelites and for the foreigner or stranger among them, so that anyone who kills a person unintentionally may flee there.","from":9},{"book":"JOS","chapter":21,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"They gave them Kiriath-arba (that is, Hebron), with its surrounding pasturelands, in the hill country of Judah. (Arba was the father of Anak.)","from":7},{"book":"JOS","chapter":21,"verse":32,"verseEnd":32,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"And from the tribe of Naphtali they were given Kedesh in Galilee (a city of refuge for the manslayer), Hammoth-dor, and Kartan—three cities, together with their pasturelands.","from":7},{"book":"1CH","chapter":6,"verse":76,"verseEnd":76,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"And from the tribe of Naphtali they were given Kedesh in Galilee, Hammon, and Kiriathaim, together with their pasturelands.","from":7},{"book":"LUK","chapter":1,"verse":39,"verseEnd":39,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"In those days Mary got ready and hurried to a town in the hill country of Judah,","from":7},{"book":"GEN","chapter":33,"verse":18,"verseEnd":19,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"After Jacob had come from Paddan-aram, he arrived safely at the city of Shechem in the land of Canaan, and he camped just outside the city. And the plot of ground where he pitched his tent, he purchased from the sons of Hamor, Shechemʼs father, for a hundred pieces of silver.","from":7},{"book":"DEU","chapter":4,"verse":43,"verseEnd":43,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Bezer in the wilderness on the plateau belonging to the Reubenites, Ramoth in Gilead belonging to the Gadites, or Golan in Bashan belonging to the Manassites.","from":8},{"book":"JOS","chapter":14,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"(Hebron used to be called Kiriath-arba, after Arba, the greatest man among the Anakim.) Then the land had rest from war.","from":7}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":5}]}}